<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<RootNamespace>DotGram.Finance</RootNamespace>
		<Description>FIX 4.4 tag-value parsing built with DotGram.</Description>

		<PackageReleaseNotes>The public surface is replaced, and 0.1.0's model is gone from the package: FixParser reads flat typed fields from a string, a byte array, a TextReader or a Stream, and FixMessages builds, validates and walks messages over the fields it is given. Wire and log framing are one enum (FixFraming); the length/data dictionary and the custom pairs are FixFieldOptions; a group comes back as its field sets rather than through typed entry classes, which are withdrawn. A streamed call takes bufferSize and maxRetained, and a field past the limit is an IOException in both the generated and the hand parser. Numbers are decimal, every public member is documented, and a package skill ships beside the README. Two breaks to know about if you are coming from 0.1.0's field reader: FixField.Unknown is now FixField.Custom, so a pattern or a cast naming the old type has to be renamed; and a supplied length/data dictionary now ADDS to the standard's sixteen pairs instead of replacing them, so a dictionary that repeated a standard pair to keep it is now refused with the tag named, and one that meant to add can drop everything it was repeating. FixFieldOptions also takes a FixCustomFields, which builds the fields of tags the package does not define; it builds field objects only, and leaves the tag unknown to the message schema.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>fix;finance;trading;parser;dotgram</PackageTags>

		<!-- The package ships its XML documentation, and every public member has some:
		     under TreatWarningsAsErrors a member left undocumented fails the build. -->
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

		<DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
		<ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
		<EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>true</EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>
		<CompilerGeneratedFilesOutputPath>$(BaseIntermediateOutputPath)GeneratedFiles</CompilerGeneratedFilesOutputPath>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Finance.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Handwritten" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Finance.Fix44" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Finance.Fix44.Tests" />

		<ProjectReference Include="../DotGram/DotGram.csproj" OutputItemType="Analyzer" ReferenceOutputAssembly="false" />

		<AdditionalFiles Include="Fix/*.gram" />

		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />

		<!-- The skill beside it, so that an agent working in a project that has restored
		     this package can read how to use it without leaving the machine. The README
		     says where it is, in a comment nothing renders. -->
		<None Include="SKILL.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />

		<None Include="../../LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="licenses/DotGram/" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Memory" />
		<PackageReference Include="Meziantou.Polyfill" PrivateAssets="all" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
